No. Donkey Kong.

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:56.060
OK. Just checking.

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:59.460
There's no bathroom breaks when you're trying to save the world, Sean.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:00.820
That's true.

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:01.920
So why don't you put that on a poster?

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:04.180
Let's do it.

00:16:04.220 --> 00:16:12.980
Why not? March. Well, so our team here of six are trying to not necessarily save the world, but save these hostages.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:19.720
And after they move on from the sniper portion, you then have to repel down these buildings.

00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:30.920
And it's funny because this was the only instance I could think of where the controls weren't as intuitive as they should have been, because I did have to go look at the manual and be like, huh?

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:33.180
Wait, what makes these guys go?

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:39.920
Because if you go down, you just repel down to, you know, to your fall and then die.

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:49.580
You have to go down and then quickly tap the up button on the D-pad to then tap your feet against the wall of the buildings.

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:53.500
This way you're actually repelling down, working with gravity.

00:16:53.500 --> 00:17:04.420
Yeah. I did gather that you had to go down and then up, but I didn't gather that that was trying to simulate the, like, hitting against the wall with your feet element.

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:15.120
Yeah, I was also doing the, like, jump down, which I think you sort of jump down if you press left or left and A or something.

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:25.260
And that made me feel much cooler because you usually see people jumping off of walls when they repel down and not just, like, slowly inching their way down.

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:30.780
But that did take me a minute to figure out because I actually didn't look at the manual for this game at all.

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:36.440
So I was just button mashing for a while and I lost some guys.

